1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,450
This is the implementation demo for journey seven.

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:07,510
It is the real application and API running on this machine,

3
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:12,750
with synthetic people and the local payment adapter, so no real money moves.

4
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:16,750
It shows how a buyer moves or cancels a booked inspection.

5
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:21,680
The buyer opens a booked inspection and chooses reschedule.

6
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:25,200
The dialog offers the same mechanic's other free times.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,530
Submitting without choosing one asks for a new time.

8
00:00:28,530 --> 00:00:32,880
Choosing a time moves the call, and a message confirms the new time.

9
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:37,370
If the buyer changes their mind, undo puts the call back where it was.

10
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:43,150
Cancelling opens a dialog with the safe choice, keep inspection, focused.

11
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:46,840
It asks for a reason, and refuses to continue without one.

12
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:49,760
It also says what comes back: the full amount,

13
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:54,840
to the card ending in four two four two, because the call is more than two hours

14
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:55,160
away.

15
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:59,480
After cancelling, the inspection shows as cancelled with the refund,

16
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:03,860
the buttons to move or cancel are gone, and it moves to the past tab.

17
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:07,970
Moving and cancelling are safe under pressure.

18
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:12,980
If another buyer takes the time someone wants to move to, the move is refused,

19
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:15,230
and the original time stays booked.

20
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:18,130
If a cancellation is sent five times at once,

21
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:20,760
the buyer is still refunded exactly once.

22
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:26,030
A cancellation less than two hours before the call keeps a twenty five dollar fee,

23
00:01:26,030 --> 00:01:30,210
and a call that has already started cannot be moved or cancelled.

24
00:01:30,210 --> 00:01:33,230
Those rules are covered by the automated tests.

25
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:36,210
Here is what to remember.

26
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:40,610
A reschedule keeps the same mechanic and frees the old time.

27
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:45,510
A cancellation needs a reason, releases the slot, and refunds once.

28
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:48,440
Only the buyer who booked can do either.

29
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:51,880
Next, journey eight: add an additional vehicle.
